2026-11-02 08:12:58,454 - INFO - FIDELITY definition: ACC@p is the fraction of graphs whose frozen-GNN argmax on the hard top-p subgraph equals the unmasked argmax. Fidelity+@p (necessity) is the mean drop in softmax probability of that unmasked class when the hard top-p edges are removed. Fidelity-@p (sufficiency) is the mean drop when only the hard top-p edges are kept. Hard top-p keeps ceil(p * n_edges) edges, at least 1 if the graph has edges, ranked by the shared explanation score with a stable argsort, per graph. This is dxmule.scales.edges_to_keep. GCNConv self-loops are not part of the stored edge_index; the explain hook leaves those loop messages at weight 1. Ground-truth edge labels are not used. IDEA and DXMulE training objectives are different and are not fidelity.
